Section D records the accuracy posture for the Section Five Impaired driving dossier. Every knowledge fact is required to trace to its cited physical handbook page, with the cited page stating the fact. Confidence is high across the section because every rule comes from the single pinned handbook edition, and every number is spelled out in words so that the card backs read aloud exactly. The extracted text of these pages carries a font-encoding shift that garbles scattered words and several fine figures in the DUI penalty table into offset characters; the dossier author decoded the letter shift deterministically, carried every penalty whose figures print legibly, stated only the legible upper bound for the serious bodily injury fine, and omitted the fine range for DUI with death because both of its figures stayed unreadable. No value was reconstructed from memory. Handbook wording is paraphrased throughout; no official sentence, table, image or question is reproduced. Penalty amounts are stated as the pinned edition prints them; no time-variable fact beyond that edition appears, so nothing required isolation as dynamic knowledge.
